* Dachshund70 power path: USB daughterboard + mainboard (rev 1.1)
* Nets and parts follow the schematics in hardware/Dachshund70-USB and
* hardware/Dachshund70. The part models are fitted by hand to datasheet
* typicals; they are good to tens of millivolts, not to the last microamp.
*
* Parameters (set with .param before including this file):
*   VHOST   host VBUS at the port (V)        RCABLE  USB-C cable, VBUS + GND (ohm)
*   LCABLE  cable loop inductance (H)
*   RFUSE   F1 BSMD1206-075 resistance (ohm) TPLUG / TUNPLUG  plug and unplug times (s)
*   VCELL   cell open-circuit voltage (V)    RCELL   cell internal resistance (ohm)
*   BATT    1 = cell connected, 0 = no cell  SWON    1 = power switch SW1 on
*   R3      Q1 gate pull-down (ohm)          ILEAK   D8 leakage on top of the model's own (A)
*   INRF    module + display current from VDDH (A)
*   ILED    SK6812MINI-E string current with LED_EN on (A)
*   LEDON   1 = LED_EN high (U3 on)          QVTO    Q1 threshold (V, negative)

.model AO3401A VDMOS(pchan Vto={QVTO} Kp=12.5 Rd=0.01 Rs=0.01 Rb=0.05 Is=2e-12 N=1
+ Cgdmax=300p Cgdmin=60p Cgs=600p Cjo=150p)
* B5819W: fitted to about 0.32 V at 0.1 A and 0.45 V at 1 A. Its Is (20 uA) is also its reverse
* leakage at a few volts and 25 C; the datasheet only gives 1 mA max at 40 V.
.model B5819W D(Is=2e-5 N=1.43 Rs=0.05 Cjo=110p BV=40 IBV=1m)
.model PLUGSW SW(Ron=1m Roff=1e9 Vt=0.5 Vh=0.1)
* USBLC6-2SC6 VBUS-to-GND clamp: breakdown 6 V min at 1 mA, about 1 ohm above it
.model USBLC6 D(Is=1e-12 N=1 BV=6.6 IBV=1m Rs=1.0 Cjo=60p)

* ---- host and cable --------------------------------------------------------
Vhost host 0 {VHOST}
Vplugctl plugctl 0 PWL(0 0 {TPLUG} 0 {TPLUG+1u} 1 {TUNPLUG} 1 {TUNPLUG+1u} 0)
Splug host hostsw plugctl 0 PLUGSW
Lcable hostsw cab {LCABLE}
Rcable cab vbus_raw {RCABLE}
Vihost vbus_raw vbus_c 0

* ---- USB daughterboard ---------------------------------------------------------
* F1 polyfuse VBUS_RAW -> VBUS, then the 6-pin JST SH cable (pin 1) to the mainboard.
Dtvs 0 vbus_c USBLC6
Rf1 vbus_c vbus_db {RFUSE}
Rjvbus vbus_db vbus 0.07
* SW1 (PCM12) switches VBAT (pin 5) to VBAT_SW (pin 6); both cross the cable.
Rj5 vbat vbat_db 0.07
Rsw1 vbat_db vbat_swdb {SWON*0.08 + (1-SWON)*1e9}
Rj6 vbat_swdb vbat_sw 0.07

* ---- battery (J2, JST PH) ------------------------------------------------------
Vcell cell 0 {VCELL}
Vibat cell cellc 0
Rcell cellc vbat {BATT*RCELL + (1-BATT)*1e9}
C3 vbat 0 4.7u
Rvbatbleed vbat 0 1e7

* ---- mainboard power path --------------------------------------------------------
C1 vbus 0 4.7u
C2 vbus 0 4.7u
R3 vbus 0 {R3}
D8 vbus vsys B5819W
* D8's reverse leakage, only while VSYS is above VBUS.
Bleak vsys vbus I={ILEAK}*max(0, tanh((V(vsys)-V(vbus))/0.05))
* Q1 AO3401A: D = VBAT_SW, G = VBUS, S = VSYS
M1 vbat_sw vbus vsys AO3401A
C4 vsys 0 4.7u
C12 vsys 0 1u
C5 vsys 0 100n
Rvsysbleed vsys 0 1e7

* ---- U2 MCP73831-2 charger (behavioural) ---------------------------------------------
* R1 = 3.3k sets 1000 V / 3.3k = 303 mA. Charges when VDD > ~3.75 V and above
* VBAT by its headroom; tapers to 0 at 4.20 V (CV).
Bchg vbus vbat I=0.303*BATT*min(1,max(0,(V(vbus)-3.6)/0.15))*min(1,max(0,(V(vbus)-V(vbat)-0.05)/0.1))*min(1,max(0,(4.2-V(vbat))/0.03))

* ---- loads ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* nRF52840 VDDH (REG0 LDO to 3.3 V) plus the display on 3V3; input current = output current.
Bnrf vsys 0 I={INRF}*min(1,max(0,(V(vsys)-1.0)/0.5))
* the module's VBUS pin (USB regulator) and the charger's own supply current
Bvbusq vbus 0 I=0.003*min(1,max(0,(V(vbus)-3.0)/0.5))
* U3 TPS22917 (about 80 mOhm on) feeding the SK6812MINI-E string and C13-C19
Ru3 vsys led_vdd {LEDON*0.08 + (1-LEDON)*1e9}
Cled led_vdd 0 0.7u
Bled led_vdd 0 I={ILED}*min(1,max(0,(V(led_vdd)-2.7)/0.5))
Rledbleed led_vdd 0 1e6
